bluejetty:00144194:ios.description:
Helsi is your convenient 24/7 access to healthcare in Ukraine. Book doctor appointments, get online consultations, find the best lab test offers, interpret test results, store medical data in your electronic health card, and get discounts on medical services – all in one app.
What you can do in Helsi:
• Book a doctor — choose a specialist, clinic, or hospital by profile, experience, reviews, or convenient time;
• Search for a doctor, clinic, or hospital — when you need a nearby facility, family physician, pediatrician, therapist, ultrasound, or another service;
• Use your patient account 24/7 — a personal portal with medical records, visit history, referrals, declarations, and conclusions;
• Access your documents — referrals, lab results, vaccinations, and other records when they are available in the service;
• Lab test marketplace: quickly search and compare lab test options with filters by location, price, promotions, and package offers that may be up to 10% lower than average market prices;
• Lab result explanations — get clear explanations of results without extra searching;
• Health Digest — monthly offers for medical services in leading laboratories in Ukraine;
• Family scenarios — book visits for relatives, manage children’s cards, vaccination calendar, reminders, and healthy routines for children;
• Helsi+ and Helsi Plan — extra options for appointments, free-slot alerts, helpful prompts, and service updates.
Helsi helps patients who want fewer phone calls, less paperwork, and a clear patient account. You can search for doctors, book appointments, manage medical documents, lab results, and reminders — all in one place.
Helsi is a Ukrainian portal for everyday health management. It helps you stay organized, keep important medical information at hand, and build healthy routines more easily.
Important: Helsi does not diagnose, treat, cure, or prevent diseases, and it does not replace consultation with a qualified medical professional. For medical advice, diagnosis, or treatment, contact a qualified healthcare professional.

